        "narrative": "<p>ALL LAKE TROUT BUT FOUR WERE CHECKED FOR CLIPS AND PIGMENT MARKING BY THE ASSESSMENT CREW. LAKE TROUT ABUNDANCE AND AVERAGE SIZE ARE GOOD. THE STRONGEST YEAR-CLASS APPEARS TO BE 1983. OF THE 15 FISH SAMPLED FROM THE 1983 YEAR-CLASS (AGE IV+) FIVE HAD PECTORAL CLIPS. FOUR OF THE FISH WITH PETORAL CLIPS HAD READABLE FLOURESCENT GREEN PIGMENT MARKS. THE PRESENCE OF AGE III, AND V AND UNMARKED AGE IV FISH INDICATED SUBSTANTIAL NATURAL REPRODUCTION. LAKE TROUT GROWTH IS SLOW BY STATE- WIDE STANDARDS. SMALLMOUTH BASS NUMBERS ARE STILL FAIRLY GOOD, ALTHOUGH THERE MAY HAVE BEEN SOME DECLINE SINCE 1984. NO LARGER SMALLMOUTH BASS WERE TAKEN IN THIS ASSESSMENT. GROWTH RATES FOR SMALL- MOUTH BASS ARE SLOW BY STATE STANDARDS. THE FORAGE BASE FOR LAKE TROUT AND SMALLMOUTH BASS APPEARS TO BE COMPOSED MAINLY OF INVERTEBRATES, ALTHOUGH MINNOWS AND SOME YELLOW PERCH ARE PRESENT.</p>",
        "surveyID": "110034",
        "surveyDate": "1987-09-08",
