        "narrative": "<p>The lake trout catch was high, well above the normal range for lakes of this ecological class, and the highest observed in Daniels Lake since 1980.  Several year classes were represented in the catch, with the 1989 and 1987 year classes the strongest.  Stocked lake trout accounted for 50, 70, and 88% of the 1989, 1987, and 1985 year classes, respectively, and accounted for 54% of the total lake trout catch.  Lake trout growth was somewhat below average for this area.The catch of smallmouth bass was the lowest observed in Daniels Lake since 1980, and follows a similarly low catch in the 1987 assessment.  Catches of other fish species in this assessment were within the normal range for this lake, historically.</p>",
